          <p>
            Buy everything from a single batch if you can. A wall left half-finished for three days while you wait on another gallon ends up with a lap line where the new coat meets the old one, and in a film coating that cold joint is a weak point. Have a brush, a roller with a 3/4-inch nap and a pail of clean water ready before you open the first can.
          </p>
