          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            DRYLOK Extreme, brushed onto clean and bare masonry, is the safest single buy for most damp basements: it carries a published pressure rating, it fills block pores and nearly every store stocks it. For unpainted poured concrete that you want to keep looking the same, a penetrating sealer such as RadonSeal Plus is the better fit.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The sequence of the work matters more than the name on the can. Send roof water away from the house, scrub off the salt, patch the cracks and only then coat. A sealer applied in that order is worth what it costs; one brushed over efflorescence beside a dumping downspout seldom survives a winter.
          </p>
